      "usage": "cloud, small dust, heaven, sky.",
      "full": "H7834. shachaq שַׁ֫חַק noun masculine Prov 9:20 dust, cloud (as fine, thin); — ׳שׁ absolute Psa 89:7 ; 89:38 , construct Isa 40:15 ; plural שְׁחָקִים Deut 33:25 +; — 1 fine dust , ׳שׁ מאֹזְנַיִם Isa 40:15 (simile of insignificance). 2 (thin) cloud , usually plural (often || שָׁמַיִם ), Deut 33:26 (poem), Isa 45:8 ; Jer 51:9 ; Job 35:5 ; 36:28 ; 37:21 ; 38:37 ; Psa 36:6 ; 57:11 ; 68:35 ; 77:18 ; 78:23 ; 108:5 ; opposed to תְּהוֺם Prov 3:20 ; 8:28 ; שׁ ׳עָבֵי 2Sam 22:12 = Psa 18:12 ; = heavens, sky Job 37:18 (with חִרְקִיעַ ), and (singular) Psa 89:7 ; 89:38 . שִׁחֹר see שִׁיחוֺר .",
